Given a sentence, , print each word of the sentence in a new line.

Input Format

The first and only line contains a sentence, .

Constraints

Output Format

Print each word of the sentence in a new line.

Sample Input 0

This is C 

Sample Output 0

This
is
C

Explanation 0

In the given string, there are three words ["This", "is", "C"]. We have to print each of these words in a new line.

Sample Input 1

Learning C is fun

Sample Output 1

Learning
C
is
fun

Sample Input 2

How is that

Sample Output 2

How
is
that
Test against custom input

SOLUTION:
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    char s[1001];
    // Read the entire line, including spaces
    fgets(s, sizeof(s), stdin);
    
    // Remove trailing newline character if present
    int length = strlen(s);
    if(s[length - 1] == '\n') {
        s[length - 1] = '\0';
    }

    // Use strtok to split the string by spaces
    char *word = strtok(s, " ");
    
    while(word != NULL) {
        printf("%s\n", word);
        word = strtok(NULL, " ");
    }

    return 0;
}


   
